EQUESTED (code=APPROVED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\\n\\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-14T15:26:30Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\\n\\nBranch `issue-463-conditioned-pasting-defect` onto `issue-455-nondegenerate-pasting-distribution`; merge base `d8bb9efb9760348c9bb9c85019549bcbda593df9`; head `7bd5558d489e404ee8631b779ca73ec1896810fd`.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\\n\\n<!-- findings:begin -->\\n- [ ] F1 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Points/WitnessMarginals.lean:37` \u2014 Add separate blueprint nodes for the two new public marginal-distance theorems.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/SupportMass.lean:41` \u2014 Add separate blueprint nodes for the two new public support-mass comparison theorems.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\n- [ ] F3 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:2682` \u2014 Correct the proof dependency: Lean calls the padded-state quadratic-form lemma, not `lem:ground-compress-effect`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1086` \u2014 Add the restricted-average and consistency-integrand positivity results actually used by the conditioned-defect proof.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\n- [ ] F5 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:367` \u2014 Record `lem:qld-decoder-linearity` in the proof dependencies for bounded encodings.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT.lean:92` \u2014 Replace the banned \u201cre-exported\u201d and namespace/import prose with mathematical wording.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\n- [ ] F7 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Points/WitnessMarginals.lean:7` \u2014 Replace the Lean identifier and runtime-limit comments with mathematical prose.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\n- [ ] F8 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/SupportMass.lean:13` \u2014 Replace Lean declaration identifiers in the documentation with the corresponding mathematical statements.  <!-- lane=prose -->\\n<!-- findings:end -->\\n\\n## Code review\\n\\nThe prior F1 is resolved: `lem:qld-conditioned-pasting-defect` now provides a dedicated blueprint entry whose statement matches `consistencyDefect_nondegenerateLinePastingDist_le`.\\n\\nThe theorem correctly reconstructs the original sample order after conditioning and applies the restriction bound to a pointwise nonnegative consistency integrand. Opposite placements provide the required commutation and positivity. It is clearly presented as a formalization-only auxiliary, not as `eq:pasting-q1`, and introduces no proof-debt hypotheses or source-statement drift.\\n\\nThe additional blueprint entries reviewed match their Lean declarations, including the rounding constants and quantifier order. The replacement combined-points paper-gap note is self-contained, accurately distinguishes the field-valued proof from the source\u2019s binary-refinement route, and gives a clear fidelity verdict.\\n\\nTargeted Lean checks and `git diff --check` succeeded. The warning in `Combining/Lines.lean` comes from the unchanged `combined_line_measurement_consistency` sorry, which is explicitly documented as the known proof obligation tracked by issues #18 and #414.\\n\\n## Prose review\\n\\n**F1.** Neither `CombinedPointsWitness.marginal_X_distance_le` nor its Z analogue appears in the blueprint. Add subordinate formalization-support nodes stating the actual generality: an arbitrary combined-point witness, directed opposite placements, and squared-distance bound `4\u03b4Q`. Do not add `\\\\leanok` to `lem:qld-xz-lines`, which remains unfinished.\\n\\n**F2.** The two public support-mass comparisons are likewise absent. Add subordinate nodes under the encoding-support material, preserving their arbitrary-vector and not-necessarily-normalized-distribution generality. These nodes must remain