\\in\\mathcal A}$ and $R=\\{R_a\\}_{a\\in\\mathcal A}$ be\n+\t\tcomplete measurements on two finite-dimensional spaces, let\n+\t\t$E\\subseteq\\mathcal A$, and suppose $R_a=0$ for every $a\\notin E$.\n+\t\tFor every vector $\\ket\\psi$ in the tensor product, without a normalization\n+\t\tassumption,\n+\t\t\\[\n+\t\t\t\\sum_{a\\notin E}q_\\psi(M_a\\ot\\Id)\n+\t\t\t\\leq \\sum_{a\\ne b}q_\\psi(M_a\\ot R_b).\n+\t\t\\]\n+\t\\end{lemma}\n+\t\\begin{proof}\n+\t\t\\leanok\n+\t\tUse completeness of $R$ to expand each term on the left as a sum over its\n+\t\toutcomes. When $a\\notin E$, the diagonal term vanishes by the support\n+\t\thypothesis. Every remaining quadratic form is nonnegative, so restricting\n+\t\tthe first outcome to $a\\notin E$ can only decrease the full off-diagonal\n+\t\tsum.\n+\t\\end{proof}\n+\n+\t\\begin{lemma}[Formalization support for averaged mass outside a supported reference measurement]\n+\t\t\\label{lem:qld-supported-reference-average-mass}\n+\t\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.avg_mass_outside_support_le_consistency_defect}\n+\t\t\\leanok\n+\t\t\\uses{def:consistency, def:distance-state-quadratic-form}\n+\t\tLet $\\mu$ be any finite-support nonnegative weighting on a finite question\n+\t\tset, not necessarily of total mass one. For each question $x$, let $M^x$\n+\t\tand $R^x$ be complete measurements with common finite outcome set\n+\t\t$\\mathcal A$, and suppose $(R^x)_a=0$ for every $a\\notin E$. Then, for\n+\t\tevery vector $\\ket\\psi$ and without a normalization assumption,\n+\t\t\\[\n+\t\t\t\\operatorname{Avg}_{x\\sim\\mu}\n+\t\t\t\\left(\\sum_{a\\notin E}q_\\psi(M^x_a\\ot\\Id)\\right)\n+\t\t\t\\leq\n+\t\t\t\\operatorname{Avg}_{x\\sim\\mu}\n+\t\t\t\\left(\\sum_{a\\ne b}q_\\psi(M^x_a\\ot R^x_b)\\right).\n+\t\t\\]\n+\t\tThe right-hand side is the bipartite consistency defect of the two\n+\t\tmeasurement families.\n+\t\\end{lemma}\n+\t\\begin{proof}\n+\t\t\\leanok\n+\t\t\\uses{lem:qld-supported-reference-point-mass}\n+\t\tApply Lemma~\\ref{lem:qld-supported-reference-point-mass} at each question\n+\t\tand average the resulting inequalities with the nonnegative weights of\n+\t\t$\\mu$.\n+\t\\end{proof}\n+\n \t\\begin{lemma}[Evaluation splits over the two Pauli answers]\n \t\t\\label{lem:qld-encoding-pauli-eval}\n \t\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.ProjectiveSetting.encodingPauliMeas_postprocess_eval}\n"},"recording_note":"Recovered after owner interruption. Artifact hashes and exact committed patch/heads verified; these are author/recovery receipts, not independent approval. Failed checks remain in raw logs. Main did not redo the mathematical assessment."}
results/telemetry/native-reviews/pr601-85b9792f-opus-20260918/prestatus.jsonl:1:{"at": "2026-09-18T09:44:14.966392+00:00", "pr": 601, "head": "85b9792fa7f7d26508bfd48efcc2718cc510a22b", "review": {"id": 5246303210, "node_id": "PRR_kwDOUJyJf88AAAABOLQ76g", "user": {"login": "Dengnifer", "id": 89234078, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg5MjM0MDc4", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89234078?u=7a60297a751d9142f3705fd4d6c15e08cfe00d0f&v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "mipstarre-review pr=601 head=85b9792fa7f7d26508bfd48efcc2718cc510a22b\n<!-- mipstarre-review pr=601 head=85b9792fa7f7d26508bfd48efcc2718cc510a22b -->\n# Review - PR 601 @ 85b9792fa7f7d26508bfd48efcc2718cc510a22b\n\nIndependent review by a Claude Opus helper (owner-authorized 2026-09-17); no author, fixer or prior reviewer context reused. Trusted prompt, persona and policy ref: 61d0ab1e21673dd6b6a729b62e28248bbad1f777. A 7-file, 422-insertion statement realignment against base `main` (merge base 2e253049): the approximate symmetrization form is proved in a new module, the printed exact-attainment theorem is left untouched as an open source gap, and the blueprint, gap note, register and an audit record the realignment.\n\n## Findings\n\n- none\n\n## Review\n\nNo earlier marked review exists on this PR, so nothing prior had to be re-checked; this is round 1.\n\n(a) Faithfulness of the approximate statements. `references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:94-99` states `val*(G) = 1 - eps`, `eps >= 0`, conclusion `val*(G,S) >= 1 - eps`; lines 101-132 prove only \"by definition for any eps' > eps there exists a strategy ... val*(G,S') >= 1 - eps'\" followed by Naimark dilation and the value-preserving symmetrization. `exists_symmetric_projective_strategy_approx` (MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/Symmetrization.lean:151-162) reproduces that second column binder for binder: `hA : Nonempty G.Answer`, `_hε : 0 ≤ ε`, `h : G.toGame.value = 1 - ε`, `hlt : ε < ε'`, conclusion `∃ S : SymmetricStrategy G, S.toStrategy.IsProjective ∧ 1 - ε' ≤ S.toStrategy.value`. I traced the proof term by term: `exists_strategy_lt_value` is `exists_lt_of_lt_csSup` on `sSup (Set.range Strategy.value)` (the literal unfolding of `Game.value`, MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/Defs.lean:556-557), the chosen `S₀` satisfies `G.value - δ < S₀.value`, and main's `exists_symmetric_projective_strategy_of_strategy` is applied at `ε := 1 - S₀.value`, which makes its hypothesis `1 - (1 - S₀.value) ≤ S₀.value` trivially true and returns `S.value = S₀.value`. No compactness, no limit, no closure of a strategy family, no attainment: the only supremum fact used is `exists_lt_of_lt_csSup`, which is strictly the \"there exists a strategy above a strict lower bound\" step of the source. The slack form `exists_symmetric_projective_strategy_of_lt_value` (:123-137) and the eps' form are interderivable under `h`, as the blueprint claims.\n\nNecessity of `Nonempty G.Answer`, checked independently of PR 540: `Game.value` is a totalized `sSup` over `Set.range (Strategy.value)`, so on an empty answer alphabet - where no `Strategy` exists, since a `Measurement` over an empty outcome type cannot sum to `1` on a space carrying a unit vector - the value is `sSup ∅ = 0` and the printed conclusion is false at `ε = 1`. The hypothesis is therefore a genuine boundary condition, and it is exactly the class `AGENTS.md:251-252` calls a faithful encoding (\"nonemptiness of a finite type\"). It is displayed in both statements, both docstrings, the blueprint node and the gap note, and it buys nothing beyond nonemptiness of the value set: `nonempty_strategy_of_nonempty_answer` only produces the one-dimensional deterministic strategy on `Unit ⊗ Unit`, so no dimension bound, no optimality and no attainment is smuggled in through it.\n\n(b) The retained printed theorem. The block `theorem exists_symmetric_projective_strategy ... sorry` is byte-identical to `github/main` (md5 of the statement-through-`sorry` span matches on both sides). Its docstring still carries the `**Unfaithful:**` marker, updated only to name tracker 524 in place of 98 (98 is indeed in the closed state, reason completed) and to record the empty-answer defect. Blueprint `lem:symmetric-strat` is unchanged and carries neither statement nor proof `\\leanok`; one sentence was appended to its proof paragraph pointing at the new node and repeating that the exact form stays an open gap. The register row and the gap note keep exact attainment open and make no completeness claim.\n\n(c) `exists_symmetric_projective_strategy_of_strategy` is unchanged against `github/main` apart from being followed by one extra blank line; its proof, statement and docstring are identical.\n\n(d) Module split: `git diff 554fc904 27219427` shows the relocated text is character-identical to what was deleted from `StrategyClasses.lean`, with only a new module docstring and `open`/`namespace` preamble added. `StrategyClasses.lean` goes 920 -> 927 lines while 920 + 138 would have passed the 1000-line guard, so the split motive checks out. `Symmetrization.lean` imports only `StrategyClasses`, and `MIPStarRE/QPBT.lean` imports it next to `StrategyClasses`; no cycle is possible and `lake env lean` on both touched files succeeds (the sole warning is the pre-existing `sorry` at StrategyClasses.lean:892).\n\n(e) `#print axioms` from a probe file outside the worktree, elaborated against the worktree at this head: `Strategy.value_le_one`, `bddAbove_range_strategy_value`, `Strategy.value_le_game_value`, `nonempty_strategy_of_nonempty_answer`, `exists_strategy_lt_value`, `exists_symmetric_projective_strategy_of_lt_value`, `exists_symmetric_projective_strategy_approx` and `exists_symmetric_projective_strategy_of_strategy` each depend on exactly `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`; `exists_symmetric_projective_strategy` still depends on `sorryAx`. No `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom` or `native_decide` is introduced.\n\n(f) Blueprint. `lem:symmetric-strat-approx` (ch12_qpbt_games.tex:140-156) matches the Lean statement quantifier by quantifier - nonempty answer alphabet, `val*(G) = 1 - eps` with `eps >= 0`, \"for every eps' > eps\", conclusion `>= 1 - eps'` - and its proof paragraph describes the exact Lean route (nonempty value set, bounded above by one, supremum property, then the given-strategy lemma), so both `\\leanok` marks are honest. Its \"formalization-only node is not a named statement of the paper\" framing follows the existing `lem:symmetric-strat-given-strategy` precedent, and naming a Lean declaration in `\\texttt{}` inside blueprint prose is established house style in this repository (ch04, ch10). `local-ci/blueprint-sync`, `blueprint-render`, `paper-gaps`, `proof-debt`, `proof-evasion`, `file-length` and `build` are all green at this exact head (`local-ci/summary`: all gating steps passed, 376s), confirming (h).\n\n(g) The unused `_hε : 0 ≤ ε` binder: acceptable, not a finding. Keeping the paper's side condition makes the Lean statement recognizable against the printed lemma and only weakens the theorem, and the underscore keeps the linter honest rather than silencing it. Dropping it would be a quiet strengthening that no longer