ems.TensorConsistency` to the `MIPStarRE.QPBT` aggregate - because the 207-line `TensorConsistency.lean` packet this PR was opened for is already on main, byte-identical.\n\n## Findings\n\n- none\n\n## Review\n\n**Scope.** `base=$(git merge-base github/main 7d5a9d5a)` = `55a94e7850c04dc9979ce840e889a07c87333f29`; `git diff --stat $base 7d5a9d5a` is `MIPStarRE/QPBT.lean | 1 +`. The branch's own commits (`00f97f6f`, `d5da7fe0`, `53bef554`, `84c7ec43` plus three main merges) predate main's own `9042eabb`, which already carries `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/DistanceTheorems/TensorConsistency.lean`; `git diff github/main 7d5a9d5a` on that path is empty. No blueprint TeX, `docs/paper-gaps`, audit or script file is touched, so the prose persona is n/a.\n\n**Prior reviews.** Four marked reviews exist (`00f97f6f`, `d5da7fe0`, `53bef554`, `84c7ec43`), each APPROVED with zero `- [ ]` entries, so no finding carries forward to this head.\n\n**Code.** I read `TensorConsistency.lean` at the published head in full even though it is main-identical, since the added import is what newly re-exports it from the aggregate. No `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom` or `native_decide`. `consistencyDefect_convolution_eq_of_perfect` is an exact identity, not a bound: `consistencyDefect` (`MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/Consistency.lean:21`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:232-248`) is the off-diagonal defect, and the proof derives the diagonal normalization `hdiag` from `point_defect_eq` rather than assuming it. The two standing hypotheses are non-trivializing: `hφ : ‖φ‖ = 1` is normalization of the ancillary state, and `hperfect` says the ancillary joint off-diagonal mass vanishes - it constrains `R`, `T`, `φ` only, and does not force the conclusion, which is proved through the genuine factorization `stateQForm_prodShuffle_vecTensor_heteroKron` and the shift-invariance argument in `sum_convolution_off_diagonal_eq`. The docstring states plainly that this is a formalization-only auxiliary, that it is not `lem:qld-