ent\n   representatives absent a degree restriction.\n2. In `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex`, adapt the checkpoint's\n   `lem:combined-point-distance-support` **after** main's field-valued\n   commutation node and **before** `lem:qld-4-10` (the old\n   `def:combined-point-sandwich` dependency is no longer a main label).\n   Retain its four mathematical assertions, the five exact `\\lean{}`\n   references, statement/proof `\\leanok`, the stated `0<=ε<=1` and `C0>=1`\n   conditions, and the `\\uses{lem:combined-point-distance-support}` edge in\n   the existing proof of `lem:qld-4-10`. Replace obsolete dependencies with\n   existing main nodes (`def:povm-distance`, `def:povm-conventions`,\n   `def:expanded-point-measurement`, `def:expanded-state`, `fact:triangle`);\n   do not duplicate the source-labelled point lemma. Confirm exact theorem\n   signatures against the current main code before adding completion tags.\n3. In the same chapter, add the surviving raw theorem\n   `MIPStarRE.QPBT.ProjectiveSetting.combinedLineMeasurement_effect_eq_pastedMeasurement`\n   to existing `lem:concrete-paired-line-degree-support` (or an explicit\n   short orientation-support entry), state `G1=Z,G2=X`, with outcome order\n   `(fZ,fX)`, and put the appropriate dependency on\n   `def:concrete-paired-line-measurement`. The existing X/Z-degree lemma stays\n   source-faithful; add no consistency claim to this orientation entry.\n4. Port the one-sentence checkpoint introduction to\n   `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Points.lean`, and replace the two\n   implementation-focused phrases at main chapter 14:1808 and 1911 with\n   the checkpoint's mathematical wording. Do not revert main's separate\n   linear-error node, current gap note, or its proved consistency chain.\n5. Optionally tidy the **proof-engineering-only** checkpoint improvement in\n   `Points/Closeness.lean`: it reused\n   `DistanceCalculus.sum_norm_sub_apply_sq_le_four` for the uniform bound,\n   whereas main again has a local `sum_norm_apply_sq_le_one` and duplicates\n   the pointwise estimate. This is not required for mathematical preservation\n   or a reason to import the checkpoint wholesale; any code port must be\n   checked against main's current imports.\n\n**Next action:** assign the small current-main support/prose packet above,\nvalidate blueprint links on *its new head*, then reconsider PR 398 as\nsuperseded specifically with the five-declaration proof correspondence and\nthe source/conditional distinction recorded here. Do not infer source\ncompletion, CI success, review approval, or publishability from this audit.\n\n## Checks and limits\n\nRead the primary paper mirror before the blueprint and Lean comparisons;\nread issue #395, public PR #398 and its latest review through primary\n`local/bin/gh_common.py`. Read trusted policy from pinned main's `AGENTS.md`,\n`local/README.md`, `local/DESIGN.md` and `local/personas/scout.md` with\n`git show`. Compared exact blobs, targeted `git diff`, `git grep`, and the\npost-review author repair note at checkpoint\n`audits/2026-09-09_pr398-third-review-repair.md`. The preserved worktree was\nclean at entry and final read. The primary checkout showed concurrent\ntelemetry-only modifications at final read; none were touched or treated as\npublished main. Static `git grep` over the four relevant main\nLean modules found no `sorry`/`axiom` text (exit 1). Main contains many\nother open paper obligations; this is no global proof-hole check. No Lean\nprobe, olean compatibility assertion, build, CI, rendering, gate, GitHub\nmutation, tracked/ref/cache edit, or other-worktree inspection was done.\nThe checkpoint's historic build and failed guarded publication recorded in\nits author audit are not current-main validation or a new review verdict.\n\nInput brief: `/tmp/qpbt-pr398-preservation-audit-20260917.md`, SHA-256\n`fe2922c35da9c50e3f7096386ff542a69387d15c9260bc04a3010a6e2a33abe5`.\nReport SHA-256 is recorded externally after writing to av