results/telemetry/native-reviews/pr597-bd62336b-opus-20260918/status.jsonl:1:{"at": "2026-09-18T08:31:52.026489+00:00", "pr": 597, "head": "bd62336b818179a59e1cda7f7b1a74197d0e6d8e", "review": {"id": 5245729575, "node_id": "PRR_kwDOUJyJf88AAAABOKt7Jw", "user": {"login": "Dengnifer", "id": 89234078, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg5MjM0MDc4", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89234078?u=7a60297a751d9142f3705fd4d6c15e08cfe00d0f&v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "mipstarre-review pr=597 head=bd62336b818179a59e1cda7f7b1a74197d0e6d8e\n<!-- mipstarre-review pr=597 head=bd62336b818179a59e1cda7f7b1a74197d0e6d8e -->\n# Review - PR 597 @ bd62336b818179a59e1cda7f7b1a74197d0e6d8e\n\nIndependent review by a Claude Opus helper (owner-authorized 2026-09-17); no author, fixer or prior reviewer context reused. Trusted prompt, persona and policy ref: 2e25304971b70661bc990bbcddefbcde6edd0bd6. One Lean file, +167/-4, one commit: it discharges the `sorry` of `marginalPoly_sub_pointMeas_approx_zero` (Equation `eq:qld-sg-cons2`) with three new private helpers and no statement change.\n\n## Findings\n\n- none\n\n## Review\n\nScope: merge-base 2e253049 (equal to the tip of `github/main`, so the branch is current) to head bd62336b; base branch is `main`. The whole main-relative change is `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Extraction/Consistency.lean`; no blueprint, docs, audit or script file is touched, so the `lem:qld-constructing-the-paulis-helper` node keeps its two `\\lean{}` tags, its `\\leanok` and its `\\uses{}` list unchanged, and prose review is n/a. No earlier marked review exists on this PR at any head.\n\nStatement integrity. The signature of `MIPStarRE.QPBT.marginalPoly_sub_pointMeas_approx_zero` at Consistency.lean:719-731 is byte-identical to `main`'s at 636-648: same universal `∃ C, 1 ≤ C ∧ ∀ P epsilon deltaG, 0 ≤ epsilon → epsilon ≤ 1 → 0 ≤ deltaG → ...`, same `opFamilyDistSq ... ≤ deltaConstructPaulis C epsilon deltaG P.m P.d P.q`, no added hypothesis, no weakened constant, and the constant is still quantified before every parameter and strategy. The only non-proof edit is the docstring: the `**Proof obligation:** issue #47` paragraph is replaced by a three-sentence description of the route (Consistency.lean:713-718). `main` carried two `sorry`s in this file (:649, :697); the head carries one (:860, `nonencodingMarginalMass_le`), which is a different, separately tracked obligation and is untouched here.\n\nFaithfulness to the source. Paper `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1637-1662` and the blueprint proof give three steps, and the Lean proof performs all three, reordering only the register move and the left multiplication (both are the same inequality chain, and doing the move before the multiplication is sound because the left factor contracts). Step 1: `marginalPoly_pointMeas_consistent_opposite` (:658) assembles the module's four existing witness consistencies over `Placement.IsOpposite` - I checked the four branches individually: `(AA',BA'')→_alice`, `(BA'',AA')→_bob_reversed`, `(BB',AB'')→_bob`, `(AB'',BB')→_alice_reversed`, each matching the placement/side pairing of the target lemma, which is the source's \"symmetric equivalents\" clause (`def:symmetric-equivalents`). `marginalPoly_pointMeas_approx_opposite` (:678) converts it at factor two through `opFamilyDistSq_le_two_mul_consistencyDefect` (`fact:agreement`, Calculus.lean:32). Step 2: `expPoint_self_cons` (Observables/PointConsistency.lean:717) supplies `C₀ * epsilon` for the same-`W` point measurement across the opposite pair; the proof flips its orientation with `opFamilyDistSq_symm` and combines by `opFamilyDistSq_le_of_le_of_le` (Calculus.lean:263, `fact:triangle`), giving exactly `2*(2*deltaG) + 2*(C₀*epsilon)`. Step 3: `opFamilyDistSq_mul_funIndexed_le` (Calculus.lean:197, `fact:add-a-proj2`) absorbs the left projective factor; its `hS` hypothesis `(1 - ∑ g, (S x g)ᴴ * S x g).PosSemidef` is discharged honestly from Hermitianness plus idempotence of the placed marginal effects and `Measurement.sum_eq_one`, i.e. the source's \"$\\hat S^W_{[g(u)=a]} \\le \\Id$\", with no conclusion-shaped or trivializing side condition. `place_marginalPoly_mul_postprocess_effect` (:626) is the paper's expansion step: projectivity collapses the fiber sum to the single matching polynomial outcome, via `place_finsetSum` and `projective_effect_mul_effect_eq_zero`. The closing arithmetic is sound: `deltaConstructPaulis C eps dG m d q = C*(dG + sqrt eps + md/q)`, `C = 4 + 2*C₀ ≥ 6 ≥ 1`, and `4*dG + 2*C₀*eps ≤ C*(dG + sqrt eps + md/q)` uses `epsilon ≤ sqrt epsilon`, which is justified by the theorem's own unchanged `0 ≤ epsilon` and `epsilon ≤ 1` hypotheses - no admissible-parameter assumption is stretched, and all three hypotheses are genuinely used.\n\nReuse and duplication. The three helper names are absent from `github/main` (`git grep` over `MIPStarRE/**` at 2e253049 returns nothing for any of them), and each is `private`, so CONTRIBUTING §5.9 does not require a blueprint support node. Every reused declaration exists on `main` with the statement the proof needs: `expPoint_self_cons`, `opFamilyDistSq_le_two_mul_consistencyD